---
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import IndustryLayout from '@/layouts/IndustryLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do you make MCB springs?',
    a: 'Yes. Switchgear and MCB springs are a regular job, inside our 0.40–2.50 mm wire range, to your drawing or sample.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What material do switch springs usually use?',
    a: 'Hard-drawn spring steel when the mechanism stays dry. Stainless 302 / 304 if the housing can damp or if the spec names stainless.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the minimum order?',
    a: `Usually ${site.terms.moq}. Smaller development runs are charged.`,
  },
];
---

<IndustryLayout
  route="switchgear"
  title="Switchgear Springs, Pune"
  description="MCB and switchgear springs, wire Ø 0.40–2.50 mm, made to drawing or sample in Talawade, Pune. Quote within 24 hours."
  h1="Electrical and switchgear springs"
  lede="MCB and switch-mechanism springs are a regular job in this shop. Wire 0.40–2.50 mm, to your drawing or an unused sample."
  context="switchgear springs"
  faqs={faqs}
  related={[
    { to: 'torsion', label: 'Torsion springs', description: 'Common in switch levers.' },
    {
      to: 'doubleTorsion',
      label: 'Double torsion springs',
      description: 'Balanced torque on a hinge.',
    },
    { to: 'extension', label: 'Tension / extension springs', description: 'Returns and trips.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>MCB and switch mechanisms</h2>
  <p>
    We make springs for <strong>electrical and switchgear</strong> assemblies, including MCB
    mechanisms. That is confirmed work, not a guess from a keyword list.
  </p>
  <p>
    Typical parts in this wire range are torsion springs on a lever, double torsion springs on a
    small hinge, extension springs on a trip or return, and short compression springs under a
    contact or a button. Wire forms show up as clips and retainers.
  </p>

  <h2>What matters on a switch spring</h2>
  <p>
    The spring has to fit a tight pocket and hold a load after many operations. Give us the hole or
    the pin, the free and working positions, and the load or torque at those positions. Wind
    direction on a torsion spring is not optional — the mechanism will fight you if it is wrong.
  </p>
  <p>
    Hard-drawn spring steel is the everyday material when the box stays dry. Stainless 302 / 304 if
    the housing can take moisture. We do not plate in-house; say the finish on the drawing and we
    send it out.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Send the drawing or the old spring. We quote within 24 hours. Usual minimum {site.terms.moq}.
    For a new part we make a development sample so you can try it in the mechanism. Dispatch is
    ex-works Talawade.
  </p>
</IndustryLayout>
